{"name":"Mahogany Rose","hex":"#c39d90","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mahogany","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The valuable wood of any of various tropical American evergreen trees, of the genus Swietenia, mostly used to make furniture. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Any of the trees from which such wood comes."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of mahogany.","Having the colour of mahogany; dark reddish-brown."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mahogany"},{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mahogany","blocks":[{"text":"Mahogany is a straight‑grained, reddish‑brown timber produced by three tropical hardwood species of the genus Swietenia, native to the Americas and belonging to the pantropical chinaberry family, Meliaceae. The term refers specifically to wood from Swietenia macrophylla, Swietenia mahagoni, and Swietenia humilis. Of these, S. macrophylla is the most widespread and the only species widely grown commercially."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Genuine_Mahogany_veneer_with_ripple_marks.jpg/330px-Genuine_Mahogany_veneer_with_ripple_marks.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahogany","wikidata":"Q239788"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose","wikidata":"Q34687"},{"title":"Mahogany (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Mahogany is a reddish-brown color. It is approximately the color of the wood mahogany. However, the wood itself, like most woods, is not uniformly the same color and is not recognized as a color by most."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mahogany_(color)","wikidata":"Q958012"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)","wikidata":"Q533047"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Swietenia_macrophylla_%2830680883066%29.jpg/500px-Swietenia_macrophylla_%2830680883066%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Swietenia_macrophylla_%2830680883066%29.jpg/500px-Swietenia_macrophylla_%2830680883066%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Honduran mahogany tree (Swietenia macrophylla)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASwietenia_macrophylla_(30680883066).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/28/Fruit_with_leaves_at_Branch_Canopy_I_IMG_8673.jpg/500px-Fruit_with_leaves_at_Branch_Canopy_I_IMG_8673.jpg?utm_source=en.wikip